This PR allows html widgets to be embedded as iframes. It works by saving the widget to html using `saveWidget` and then using `htmltools` to embed it as an iframe. 

By default, it saves the widget html to file using `selfcontained = TRUE` and then uses the [srcdoc](http://www.w3schools.com/TAgs/att_iframe_srcdoc.asp) attribute to embed it as an inline iframe. This allows the resulting html document to be selfcontained. The `srcdoc` attribute is not supported by IE, and for some reason does not appear to be supported in the Rmd previewer as well.

